The MIT grant above covers this project's own code, and the third-party code
ported into it with attribution under compatible terms.

One exception, documented in full in CREDITS.md. Five ATS provider handlers
in job_scanner.py — search_workday, search_greenhouse, search_lever,
search_ashby and search_smartrecruiters, roughly 193 lines — began as a
personal job scanner Greg Nudelman wrote for his own search and gave to the
author directly. They are published here with his written permission, which
is not the same thing as a licence he granted. Fork this repository and you
inherit the MIT grant over everything else; for those five functions, read
CREDITS.md before relying on it.
